on\n\nSecondary: 05A20: Combinatorial inequalities\n\n* * *\n\n## Information\n\nType\n    Research Article\n\nInformation\n    \n\nMathematika , Volume 20 , Issue 2 , December 1973 , pp. 208 - 209\n\nDOI: https://doi.org/10.1112/S0025579300004782 [Opens in a new window]\n\n## References\n\n1\n\n1. Daykin, D. E. and Lovasz, L., “The number of values of Boolean functions” (submitted).Google Scholar\n\n2\n\n2. Edmonds, J. and Fulkerson, D. R., “Bottleneck Extrema”, J. Combinatorial Theory, 8 (1970), 299–306.CrossRefGoogle Scholar\n\n3\n\n3. Kleitman, D. J., “Families of non-disjoint subsets”, J. Combinatorial Theory, 1 (1966), 153–155.CrossRefGoogle Scholar\n\n4\n\n4. Schönheim, J., “Ideals of sets ”, Proc. British Combinatorial Conference Aberystwyth (1973) (forthcoming).Google Scholar\n\n5\n\n5. Brace, A. and Daykin, D. E., “Spemer type theorems for finite sets ”, Combinatorics (Proc. Combinatorial Conference, Oxford, 1972).Google Scholar--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOn some percolation results of J. M. Hammersley | Journal of Applied Probability | Cambridge Core (https://www.cambridge.org/core/services/aop-cambridge-core/content/view/6EB8C591AE191D4766F5AB82707F2F69/S0021900200107673a.pdf/on_some_percolation_results_of_j_m_hammersley.pdf)\nciteturn10725search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10.2 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; [4] Edmonds, J. and Fulkerson, D. ... (1970) Bottleneck extrema.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCWI Scanprofile/PDF/300 (https://ir.cwi.nl/pub/9780/9780D.pdf)\nciteturn10725search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 19.7 years ago; Crawled: 5.6 years ago; Edmonds and D.R. ... Fulkerson, \"Bottleneck Extrema\", *J.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCombinatorial Methods and Models PDF | PDF | Combinatorics | Logarithm (https://www.scribd.com/document/363450805/Combinatorial-Methods-and-Models-pdf)